          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The Strategy That Uses All Three</h3>
          <p>
            Natural gas is the workhorse — connect it and use it for any outage lasting more than a few hours, because runtime is unlimited and there is nothing to store. Propane is the backup for the rare case where gas service is also interrupted, and it is also the right fuel for monthly exercise runs since it leaves no carburetor varnish. Gasoline is for maximum output, for deep-cold starts, and for using the generator away from the house.
          </p>

