                No. A large generator consumes many times what a grill does, and a barbecue quick-connect and its supply line are not sized for that demand. An undersized line produces a generator that starts and then stumbles under load. You need a properly sized line and fitting installed by a licensed gas fitter, using the generator's specification sheet.
